# Backend serve verification (modules / services / DI)

Whenever a backend change **adds or wires** Nest providers — new module, service, controller, guard, interceptor, or other DI registration — do not treat the task as done until the app can start locally.

## Required check

Run (and leave running long enough to confirm boot):

```bash
nx serve backend --configuration=development
```

Success means TypeScript build completes **and** Nest boots without DI / module errors (look for the usual listen / Nest application successfully started log). Fix any failure before finishing.

Prefer this over `nx build backend` alone when DI or module graphs changed — compile success does not prove providers resolve at runtime.

## Also catch declaration emit breaks

`backend:build` / serve use `@nx/js:tsc` with declaration emit. Public controller methods whose inferred return type references a **non-exported** service type fail with **TS4053** (“cannot be named”).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — ReelRow used on public service methods but not exported
interface ReelRow { id: string }

// ✅ GOOD
export interface ReelRow { id: string }
```

Export types returned (or inferred) from public Nest methods, or give controllers explicit exported return types.

## Scope reminders

- Register new services in the correct Nest module `providers` / `exports`.
- Import feature modules into `AppModule` (or a parent module) when adding a new domain module.
- Prefer existing global modules for shared infra; see `backend-nestjs-global-modules.mdc`.
- Request-scoped Hasura access: see `backend-nestjs-request-scope.mdc`.
